# the seven server programs this directory links.  their real names are
# $(SQLR)-start$(EXE) and so on - see the clean target in Makefile - where
# SQLR is the branding prefix from configure's --with-sqlr-name and
# defaults to sqlr.  a .gitignore pattern cannot expand a make variable, so
# the default names are spelled out; the .exe a windows build appends is
# covered by *.exe in src/.gitignore.  a tree branded with a different
# --with-sqlr-name shows its binaries untracked, the same machine-specific
# gap the rest of the tree accepts (#9678)
/sqlr-cachemanager
/sqlr-connection
/sqlr-listener
/sqlr-scaler
/sqlr-start
/sqlr-status
/sqlr-stop

# in a static build (SQLRELAY_ENABLE_SHARED=no) this directory's Makefile
# generates one declarations and one assignments .cpp per module type from
# the matching .cpp.in template, by globbing the module directory's object
# files at make time - config.mk.in's STATICPLUGINSRCS lists all 42.  the
# wildcards cover the pair a new module type will add too.  the .cpp.in
# templates are hand maintained and stay tracked (#9678)
/sqlr*declarations.cpp
/sqlr*assignments.cpp
